Package: TimeMetric
Type: Package
Title: Unified Performance Metrics for Survival Models with Right-Censoring,
    Competing Risks, and Two-Phase Designs
Version: 0.2.1
Date: 2026-10-18
Authors@R: c(
    person("Tong", "Zhu", email = "toz015@ucla.edu", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Zian", "Zhuang", role = "aut"),
    person("Wen", "Su", role = "aut"),
    person("Xiaowu", "Dai", role = "aut"),
    person("Gang", "Li", role = "aut"))
Description: Evaluates the predictive performance of survival models in a
    unified framework. Implements the pseudo R-squared and related explained
    variation measures of Li and Wang (2019)
    <doi:10.1080/01621459.2018.1515079>, the concordance indices of Harrell
    et al. (1982) <doi:10.1001/jama.1982.03320430047030> and Uno et al.
    (2011) <doi:10.1002/sim.4154>, the time-dependent area under the receiver
    operating characteristic curve (AUC) of Heagerty, Lumley and Pepe (2000)
    <doi:10.1111/j.0006-341X.2000.00337.x>, and the Brier score of Graf et
    al. (1999)
    <doi:10.1002/(SICI)1097-0258(19990915/30)18:17/18%3C2529::AID-SIM274%3E3.0.CO;2-5>.
    Supports right-censored data; competing risks, following Wolbers et al.
    (2014) <doi:10.1093/biostatistics/kxt059>, Wu and Li (2018)
    <doi:10.1002/sim.7806> and Zhuang et al. (2025)
    <doi:10.48550/arXiv.2507.15040>; and two-phase sampling designs such as
    case-cohort and nested case-control studies, following Lee,
    Zeleniuch-Jacquotte and Liu (2021) <doi:10.1080/02664763.2020.1861225>.
    Extends and generalizes the 'PAmeasures' package.
Depends: R (>= 4.1.0)
